  "body": "Found by the independent review of PR #278 (which fixes the single profile/contour pass exit, #229).\n\n#278 makes a turning pass that ends inside a longer bar leave its cut at feed: when the stock runs past the pass end, the exit is a feed at the plunge feed instead of a rapid through stock. But the **multi-pass, chamfer and taper** turning kinds still read no stock, so on a bar longer than the part they keep the old rapid exit - a G0 through material at the end of each pass.\n\nNot yet reproduced with a test; whether the program sim or the rapid verdict catches it today is unchecked. If nothing refuses it, it is a silent rapid-through-stock (collision class) and should be raised to P0.\n\n**Done means:** each of these kinds reads the stock like #278's pass does and exits at feed when the bar runs past its end (or refuses by name), pinned by a test per kind on a bar longer than the part; plus a test that the verifier/sim refuses a rapid exit through stock.\n\nRelated: #229, PR #278.\n",
